      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Each side of the triangle is a segment, which can intersect a circle in at most \\(2\\) points. With \\(3\\) sides, the maximum is \\(3\\cdot2=6\\) points, and this is achievable.\n\nThus, the correct answer is E.",
